# Pharmacy Patient Flow

## Purpose
Pharmacy owns encounter-linked dispensing, returns, stock visibility, and take-home medicines. Keep dispensing separate from prescribing and from ward MAR administration.

## Stage Sequence
- Order received from OPD, IPD, or discharge planning.
- Billing gate checked when required.
- Medicine prepared, verified, and attested.
- Ward delivery or patient pickup completed.
- Return processed when applicable.
- Discharge medicines prepared for exit clearance.

## Handoffs
- Doctor or clinical user owns prescription creation.
- Pharmacist owns dispense, attest, and returns.
- Nurse owns ward administration recording on IPD.
- Discharge flow owns final clearance for take-home medicines.

## Hard Invariants
- Must not create encounters or change OPD/IPD stages directly.
- Must not duplicate MAR administration in pharmacy.
- Must keep every dispense tied to the source encounter.
- Must not mix outpatient, inpatient, and discharge-pending queues.

## Allowed Critical Actions
- Use the pharmacy workbench as the canonical dispensing workspace.
- Support pay-now or bill-later at order time when policy requires it.
- Surface returns with a reason and keep stock visibility accurate.
- Prioritize discharge medicines so final clearance stays unblocked.

